B.baY=new A.cN("record",B.kV,"How do I record something?","Press REC, the record key in the bar at the foot of the four main screens: Your music, Open Mic, Messages and Learn. On a wider screen, a tablet held sideways or a computer, the bar has no REC: press New idea instead. On other screens, press More, then Everything else, then Record an idea. It starts a new idea \u2014 no naming, no choosing where it lives. You can do both afterwards, once there is something worth filing.\n\nThe first time, it asks to use the microphone. Then it counts 3, 2, 1 and records; press Start now if you are ready sooner. To record from the tap with no count, press Tools in the recorder and turn off Count in before recording.\n\nPress Stop and save when you have it. It is saved in Ideas at once, and the page shows how long it is, with Hear it, Record again (which keeps this one and starts another) and Throw away (with Undo). Done takes you back to where you were.\n\nOn a phone it works with no signal: the recording is kept on the phone first, and goes into Your music by itself when there is signal. One recording runs for up to 12 minutes, which is as long as a song here can hold, and the recorder says so in the last minute.\n\nIf the idea is words and there is nowhere quiet to sing, press Tools in the recorder and then Write it down. It is also under More on Your music, and under More in Ideas. On a phone what you type is kept on the phone as you type it, and goes into Ideas as a song named from its first line when you press Done, or by itself once there is signal.\n\nTo add a recording to a song you already have, open it and press Record it, the gold at the foot. Once the song has a recording, the same gold says Record a take. On a computer, with a song open beside Your music, the gold button says Record, or New take once the song has a recording; with no song open it says New idea.",B.cAV)
B.ewt=s(["workspace_layers_button","layers_record_button"],t.s)
B.bZy=s(["take","takes","another","add","overdub","layer","part","second","share","shared","song"],t.s)
B.bb0=new A.cN("take",B.dR,"How do I add a take to a song?","Open the song and press Record a take, the gold button at the foot (Record it, if the song has no recording yet). Takes opens, counts you in, and records over the song while it plays; press Stop when you are done. To come in partway, tap the song's bar on Takes where you want to start, and press Record from there.\n\nA take stays private to you until you share it. Tap it on Takes, press Tools, and press Share for the one you want the room to hear \u2014 nothing you have not shared is ever audible to anybody, including on the Open Mic. The same Tools takes it back, or takes it off the song.\n\nWith no signal, a take is kept on the phone and shown on Takes as On this phone, not sent yet; tap it for Try again. It goes up by itself when there is signal. If a take sounds late, tap it, press Tools, then Volume and timing, and press Line it up to move it while it plays.",B.bZy)
B.ey2=s(["workspace_analyze_button","choose_reference_recording"],t.s)
B.c72=s(["chord","chords","sheet","lyrics","words","key","tempo","bpm","transcribe","transcription","tab","analyse","analyze","notation","song"],t.s)
B.bak=new A.cN("sheet",B.dR,"How do I get the chords and words for my song?","Record something first, then open the song and press Song Sheet, and choose one.\n\nChords is free: the chords and the key, with no words or bar lines. The full analysis also writes down the words you sang and puts the chords over them, finds the tempo and the bars, and names the parts; it uses a credit, takes a few minutes, and keeps going if you leave the screen.",B.c72)
B.exH=s(["/settings/what-you-play","account_what_you_play_row","what_you_play_sheet"],t.s)
B.ctl=s(["ukulele","uke","bass","piano","keyboard","left","handed","lefty","shape","shapes","diagram","instrument","nashville","roman","sargam","jianpu","solfege","trumpet","sax","saxophone","horn","transpose","transposing","reading"],t.s)
B.b9X=new A.cN("what-you-play",B.dR,"I play a ukulele, a bass or a piano, not a guitar.","Account \u2192 Music \u2192 What you play and how you read.\n\nPick guitar, ukulele, bass or piano, and left-handed if you read a neck the other way round. Every chord diagram, sheet, chart and printed page follows it from then on. The same question is under any chord diagram and in the tuner, so you can answer it where you are.\n\nThe same screen sets how you read: chords as letters, Nashville numbers or Roman numerals; sung notes as letters, do-re-mi, fixed do, sargam or jianpu; and the written key of a transposing instrument, so a trumpet part reads in B\u266d without you moving every chord in your head.\n\nIt is kept with your account, so a new phone starts where the last one left off, and nobody else can see it \u2014 not your band, not a teacher. A song you have already set differently keeps its own setting.",B.ctl)
B.exO=s(["song_audience_dial"],t.s)
B.cab=s(["who","hear","private","privacy","public","visible","audience","secret","safe","sharing","permission","song"],t.s)
B.baZ=new A.cN("audience",B.dR,"Who can hear my song?","Open the song, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it. The row Who can hear this has the answer beside it, and tapping it shows the whole picture:\n\n\u2022 Only you \u2014 nobody else is in the room it lives in\n\u2022 Your room \u2014 everybody in that room\n\u2022 People you asked \u2014 somebody invited to this one song\n\u2022 Anyone \u2014 it is on the Open Mic\n\nYou can move it back down at any time, and a take you have not shared stays private no matter where the song sits.",B.cab)
B.ewL=s(["song_audience_dial","audience_open_mic_toggle"],t.s)
B.czo=s(["open","mic","publish","post","share","public","everybody","upload","showcase","song"],t.s)
B.baO=new A.cN("openmic",B.lS,"How do I put a song on the Open Mic?",'Open the song, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it, then Who can hear this, and "Put it on the Open Mic".\n\nAny adult signed in can then find it, listen, and offer to play on it. Only the takes your room has already heard become audible \u2014 never one you are still working on privately. The same row takes it back down whenever you like.\n\nWhoever started a song is the one who puts it up. On a song somebody else started, the same row says who that is.',B.czo)
B.cEo=s(["take","off","remove","delete","down","unpublish","hide","undo","mic","song"],t.s)
B.bai=new A.cN("takedown",B.lS,"How do I take a song off the Open Mic?",'Open the song, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it, then Who can hear this, and "Take it off the Open Mic". It stops being findable immediately.\n\nNothing you did while it was up is lost \u2014 the song, the takes and the song sheet all stay exactly as they were.\n\nWhoever started the song can take it down, and so can the room\u2019s owner.',B.cEo)
B.ewQ=s(["/openmic","/openmic/musicians","ask_song_send","open_mic_ask_somebody_not_here"],t.s)
B.csc=s(["ask","help","request","collaborate","collaborator","musician","find","bass","drummer","singer","song"],t.s)
B.ban=new A.cN("ask",B.dR,"How do I ask somebody for help on a song?",'It depends on whether you have somebody in mind, and whether they are on the app.\n\nIf they are: on the Open Mic, tap them among the people there (More, then Narrow it down, finds them by what they play), and ask them from their page. They see the one song you named and nothing else of yours until they say yes.\n\nIf they are not on the app yet: on the Open Mic, tap More, then "Invite someone you know". It writes a message about one of your songs for you to send them, and it opens that one song to them, nothing else of yours.\n\nIf you have nobody in mind: put the song on the Open Mic and say what it needs. It then shows up for people who play that part, and they can offer.',B.csc)
B.ews=s(["/notifications","ask_card_reply"],t.s)
B.cb_=s(["asked","invite","invited","invitation","notification","bell","accept","decline","yes","request","join","song"],t.s)
B.ba4=new A.cN("answer-ask",B.dR,"Somebody asked me to play on their song. Where is it?","In your notifications \u2014 the bell in the top corner. Open it and you can say yes or no.\n\nSaying yes gives you that one song, not the rest of their work. Saying no tells them and nothing else happens.",B.cb_)
B.ewP=s(["songs_new_room","your_music_tab_rooms"],t.s)
B.c7_=s(["room","rooms","band","group","folder","catalog","organise","organize","make","create","new"],t.s)
B.bam=new A.cN("rooms",B.hb,"What is a room, and how do I make one?","A room is who can see a set of songs \u2014 your band, a side project, or just the songs you write on your own. Every song lives in one, and the room decides who hears it.\n\nYour rooms are under Rooms, beside Songs and Sets, under the title of Your music. Make one there: press More, then New room. Your first song goes into Ideas, your own room, without asking; after that More, then New song, asks where it goes and can make the room on the way.",B.c7_)
B.exc=s(["roomthread_more_invite","invite_link"],t.s)
B.cej=s(["invite","add","member","bandmate","friend","room","join","collaborator","people"],t.s)
B.ba2=new A.cN("invite-room",B.hb,"How do I invite somebody to my room?","Open the room and tap Invite, beside the names under its title. Pick one of your people, or Send a link, or Show a code.\n\nA room invitation is everything in it, now and later \u2014 so if you only want somebody on one song, ask them to play on that song instead. You can also invite somebody you met on the Open Mic straight from their profile. In Messages, the room's conversation has it too: Tools, Members, then Invite somebody, to pick from your people or share a link.",B.cej)
B.exM=s(["roomthread_more_members"],t.s)
B.cwg=s(["remove","kick","member","leave","left","quit","band","delete","room"],t.s)
B.baW=new A.cN("remove-member",B.hb,"How do I remove somebody from a room?","Open the room, then the members list, and remove them there. They lose the room and every song in it.\n\nWhat they already recorded stays \u2014 a take keeps its author, and removing somebody does not erase the work they did with you.",B.cwg)
B.ewB=s(["/account","open_mic_list_me"],t.s)
B.c8B=s(["sounds","like","genre","style","taste","tags","profile","describe","match","matching"],t.s)
B.baA=new A.cN("sounds-like",B.lS,'What does "sounds like" do on my profile?','It is how the app finds people making the kind of music you make. "Guitarist" does not say whether you play metal or jazz; this does.\n\nNobody is ranked by it. It moves you sideways towards people in the same corner, never up or down past anybody. Set it on your page: on Account, tap your name, then Edit your page, then What you sound like. Five words at most \u2014 fewer and sharper works better than listing everything.',B.c8B)
B.ewq=s(["/account","open_mic_more_listed","open_mic_list_me"],t.s)
B.bEf=s(["discoverable","found","find","visible","hidden","profile","appear","listed","city","location","search","open","mic","showing"],t.s)
B.ba7=new A.cN("discoverable",B.lS,"How do I show up in the Open Mic, or stop showing up?","On the Open Mic, tap More, then Listed on the Open Mic, pick one, and press the button under it. Or Account \u2192 Privacy and safety \u2192 Listed on the Open Mic, which asks the same way. It is off until you turn it on \u2014 nobody appears in the Open Mic without choosing to.\n\nThe same page has Who sees your city: nobody, only people you have made music with, or anybody browsing.",B.bEf)
B.ewO=s(["/openmic","/openmic/notes","/openmic/musicians","open_mic_leave_want","leave_want_your_notes","leave_want_send","yourpage_more_your_notes","/account","account_your_notes_row"],t.s)
B.cai=s(["told","looking","joins","wanted","notes","left","turned"],t.s)
B.bal=new A.cN("leave-a-note",B.lS,"Can I be told when somebody I am looking for joins?",'Yes. On the Open Mic, tap More, then Notes, then "Leave a note for someone here". From Narrow it down it is at the top of the list however many people your search found. Choose who you would like to meet (if you searched for one kind of player they are already chosen), add a line for yourself if you like, and leave it.\n\nWhen somebody who plays that lists themselves on the Open Mic, you get a notification with their name, and tapping it opens their page. If you both show a town it has to be the same town, spelled the same way apart from capitals; if either of you shows none, the town does not come into it. Nobody is told who left a note.\n\nA note lasts a month. "Your notes", at the foot of the same sheet, is where you change one or take it down. It is in Account too, in More on Privacy and safety, as "Notes you left on the Open Mic", and in More on your page.',B.cai)
B.ewn=s(["songs_new_set","your_music_tab_sets","play_the_set","share_set_pdf","the_bands_sets","give_set_to_room","live_previous_in_set","live_running_order","set_carry_on"],t.s)
B.ckf=s(["set","sets","setlist","setlists","list","gig","order","practice","performance","live","dep","sub","chart","key","tempo","form","ending","play","long","length","duration","minutes","slot","print","pdf","share","make","give","bandmates"],t.s)
B.bad=new A.cN("sets",B.dR,"How do I make a set list?","In Your music, press More, then New set: name it, choose where it lives and, if you like, the day it is for, then press Make the set. Your sets are under Sets, beside Songs and Rooms.\n\nA set is a running order for one occasion \u2014 Friday practice, Saturday's show \u2014 built from songs you already have, in whatever order you will play them.\n\nEach row carries the key you do it in, the tempo, the count-in, the form, how it ends and a note. Key and notes on the row opens all six. Leave a field empty and the set uses what the song says.\n\nPlay this set walks the running order one song at a time, in the set's keys, with its tempo and notes on the stand, Previous and Next, and the recording off. Play from here starts part way down; leave a song early and Carry on takes you back to it.\n\nThe set adds up how long it runs. A length it measured from a recording and one it is working out are shown differently, and the total says how many of them are guesses. A song with nothing to go on has no length and is left out. A song whose sheet your phone has not been able to read says that instead, and the total says how many are still missing. The time between songs is never counted.\n\nHand this out gives you the three ways out of the app: print it, send the pack as a PDF with a chord chart for every song in the keys you play them in, or send the running order as text.\n\nA set can be the whole band\u2019s. Open the room: The band\u2019s sets is beside its songs. Everybody in the room sees the same running order, keys and notes on their own phone, and the room\u2019s owner and everybody who can record and edit can change it. The set says who changed it last, and never who opened it. When you open it, it fetches the latest and says what changed since your phone last had it; with no signal it shows the copy on your phone and says from when.\n\nTo make one of your own sets the band\u2019s, open it and press Give this set to the room. Every song in it has to be one of that room\u2019s songs first. From then on it is the room\u2019s: only the room\u2019s owner, or somebody who can record and edit, can give it back, from the set\u2019s Tools, under Finish, rename or delete, where the day it is for and Delete this set are too.",B.ckf)
B.exG=s(["live_recording"],t.s)
B.cpq=s(["silent","speaker","playback","backing","loud"],t.s)
B.baM=new A.cN("perform-silent",B.dR,"Can Perform be silent, with nothing coming out of the speaker?","Yes. In Perform, the switch beside Start says Recording on or Recording off; tap it. With the recording off nothing comes out of the phone, and the words still move in time with the song \u2014 the count-in, the beat you feel and the chords called out loud all carry on. Your phone remembers it.\n\nA set opens with the recording off, so on a stage only the words move, and your phone remembers what you choose for sets separately.",B.cpq)
B.exP=s(["song_keep_here","keep_set_here"],t.s)
B.cr2=s(["offline","signal","airplane","aeroplane","wifi","internet","reception","basement","van","kept","song","perform","phone","keep"],t.s)
B.ba9=new A.cN("offline",B.kV,"Can I play a song where there is no signal?","Yes, if you keep it on your phone first. Open the song, press Tools, then Finish, rename or delete, and turn on Keep on this phone. A set has Keep on this phone in its Tools, and keeps every song in it \u2014 it says how much space that will take before it takes it, and once the day a set was for has passed it offers to take those songs back off.\n\nThat fetches the words, the song sheet, the recording and its separated parts, so Perform plays the song with its chords and beats with no connection at all. The switch is then on, and a small phone sits beside the name of the song; turn the switch off to take the song off.\n\nIf the app cannot open because there is no signal, the songs you kept are listed on that screen, ready to perform, and so are the sets you have opened on this phone, as this phone last had them, ready to play in order.\n\nIt is only for you and only on this phone: nobody in the room is told, and nobody else who signs in here sees them. A song that is not kept still opens with its words, and says that the recording is missing. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a song, so Tools does not offer it there.",B.cr2)
B.ewW=s(["ideas_on_this_phone","ideas_on_this_phone_says"],t.s)
B.ccE=s(["recorded","sent","unsent","yet","waiting","upload","uploaded","uploading","plane","flight","signal","lost","phone"],t.s)
B.baG=new A.cN("not-sent-yet",B.kV,"I recorded something with no signal. Where is it?","On your phone, and safe. On Your music it is first under Ideas, saying On this phone, not sent yet, for as long as the phone is holding it.\n\nOpen it to play what you recorded, send it somewhere else with the share sheet, or delete it. Deleting removes it from the phone completely, and it was never anywhere else.\n\nYou do not have to do anything to send it. When there is signal it becomes a song in your Ideas room by itself, under the date and time you recorded it, and it takes its name from what you sang once you make its song sheet. If it cannot be sent for a reason that is not the signal, Ideas says so, and opening it says why.\n\nIf the app cannot open at all because there is no signal, the microphone button, New idea, and the same row are on that screen too. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a recording, so recording there needs a connection.",B.ccE)
B.ewG=s(["songs_search_field","songs_all_your_songs"],t.s)
B.cuk=s(["find","lost","missing","gone","cannot","disappeared","search","song","deleted"],t.s)
B.baS=new A.cN("missing-song",B.dR,"I cannot find a song I made.","Everything you have is in Your music: on Songs, under the room it lives in, and every one of them in All your songs, at the end of that list. If you cannot see it, use the search box under Songs, Rooms and Sets: it finds a song by its title or by a line of its words you remember, and a room or a set by its name.\n\nIf it was somebody else's song you were invited to, it is under their room rather than yours.",B.cuk)
B.exg=s(["call_report","roomthread_more_report_this_room"],t.s)
B.ccV=s(["report","abuse","harassment","inappropriate","offensive","spam","copyright","stolen","complaint","flag","posted"],t.s)
B.bb3=new A.cN("report",B.lS,"Somebody posted something they should not have.","Report it. There is a flag on a song's public page. On their page, press More, then Report. On a room, press Tools, then Report this room; its conversation in Messages has it in Tools too. In a call, press the dots in the corner of their picture.\n\nYou can also block somebody from their profile \u2014 you stop seeing each other completely, in both directions, and they are not told.\n\nA person reads every report, and you are told what they decided: Account \u2192 Privacy and safety \u2192 Reports you made.",B.ccV)
B.ex0=s(["/settings/reports","account_reports_row"],t.s)
B.cxq=s(["reported","reports","reporting","answered","decided","decision","moderation","moderator","reviewed"],t.s)
B.baJ=new A.cN("after-report",B.lS,"What happens after I have reported something?","It goes to a person, not a machine. If it is about sexual content or music that is not theirs, an alarm goes off on our side once it has waited a day; for anything else, two days.\n\nIf you said it was sexual content on a profile, a picture, a song or a take, it goes to the front of the queue, and we take it out of other people's sight while somebody looks. Nothing is deleted while that happens.\n\nYou are told what was decided. Open Account \u2192 Privacy and safety \u2192 Reports you made: each report shows what you wrote, that a person is looking at it, and then their answer. If whoever it belongs to deletes it first, your report is not deleted with it: you are told it is no longer here. You also get a notification when there is an answer; it says nothing about what you reported, so it is safe on a lock screen.\n\nThe person you reported is never told who reported them, and never sees what you wrote.",B.cxq)
B.exa=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row"],t.s)
B.cnf=s(["refund","money","pay","paid","payment","charge","charged","cost","price","subscription","billing","cancel","free","premium","upgrade"],t.s)
B.b9R=new A.cN("refund",B.i0,"How do I get a refund? What does this cost?","Nothing yet. Studio, the paid plan, is $9.99 a month or $99.99 a year (save $19.89 a year), when it opens. Until then nothing in CoLabRoom can be paid for, so there is nothing to refund.\n\nIf you were charged by something calling itself CoLabRoom, it was not us \u2014 tell us at support@colabroom.com and do not pay it.",B.cnf)
B.ewK=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row","what_you_get_credits","what_you_get_credit_history","analysis_depth_full"],t.s)
B.ciB=s(["credit","credits","balance","full","analysis","expire","lapse","monthly","many"],t.s)
B.baD=new A.cN("credits",B.i0,"What is a credit, and how many do I have?","A credit is one full analysis of one recording: the words, the bar lines, every instrument kept as its own track, and the song\u2019s parts named. The chords sheet, with no words or bar lines, never uses one, and running the full analysis again on a recording that has had one does not either.\n\nIn Account, Sign-in and phone has Song sheets left this month, which says how many you have, and Where your credits went lists each one. Every account starts with a few that do not expire; somebody on Studio gets more each month, and those do not carry over. If an analysis does not finish, its credit comes back by itself.\n\nThe Full analysis button says what it will use before you tap it.",B.ciB)
B.ewJ=s(["analysis_depth_full","your_credits_here","share_my_credits_here","what_you_get_credit_history"],t.s)
B.cBJ=s(["lend","lending","borrow","borrowing","use","using","let","credits","bandmates","yours","theirs"],t.s)
B.baL=new A.cN("use-one-of-mine",B.i0,"Can my band use my credits, or can I use theirs?",'Yes, in a band of up to eight, and only with a yes. If you have no credits of your own and somebody on Studio is in the song\u2019s room, the Full analysis option offers Ask and their name. One tap sends them a notification naming the song, and they see that you asked.\n\nThey answer from their inbox or the song: Just this once, Yes and let this room use mine from now on, or Not now. A yes spends one of their credits, never anybody else\u2019s, and their Where your credits went says which song and who asked.\n\nWhoever said "from now on" turns it off in the room: tap the names under its title, and it is under Your credits here, the last thing on that page. It turns itself off if the room grows past eight.',B.cBJ)
B.ewy=s(["/account","roomthread_more_members"],t.s)
B.ceW=s(["delete","account","remove","close","quit","leave","erase","data","gdpr","deactivate"],t.s)
B.bac=new A.cN("delete-account",B.i0,"How do I delete my account?","Account, then Sign-in and phone, then Delete account. It removes your profile, your words, and every room nobody else is in, with its songs. It cannot be undone.\n\nIf other people are in a room of yours, it is listed first, with two ways to settle it. Hand it over moves the room and every song in it to somebody in it, once they say yes. Close the room gives every song somebody else in it started, played on or wrote on to them, in a room of their own, and deletes the rest. Your account can be deleted once each room is settled.\n\nSongs you started and takes you shared in other people's rooms stay with their bands, without your name.",B.ceW)
B.ewX=s(["roomthread_more_leave","hand_over_offer"],t.s)
B.cuJ=s(["hand","handover","transfer","owner","ownership","give","role","permission","editor","viewer","commenter","promote","demote","admin","leader","band"],t.s)
B.bb2=new A.cN("hand-a-room-over",B.hb,"How do I hand a room over, or change what somebody can do?","Both are on the room\u2019s list of people. Open the room and tap the line under its name that says how many people are in it.\n\nUnder each person there is Change what they can do \u2014 record and edit, comment, or listen. It takes nothing away from them: their sets, their takes and the songs they are on all stay.\n\nUnder each person there is also Hand the room to them. They have to say yes: a card appears in their room and in their inbox, and nothing moves until they take it on. You can take the offer back until they answer, and it stops being offered after a fortnight.\n\nWhen they accept, the room and every song in it become theirs. You stay on and can still record and edit, unless you ticked Leave the room when they accept. Song sheets are counted against whoever makes them, so neither of your allowances changes.\n\nIf they already have a room or a song with the same name, the app says which and waits: one of them has to be renamed first. Nothing is ever renamed for you.\n\nBoth of you keep the same dated line about it on that list of people, and only the owner can hand a room on.",B.cuJ)
B.exB=s(["/openmic"],t.s)
B.ca1=s(["demo","fake","bot","test","real","account","label","chip","seeded","nobody"],t.s)
B.bas=new A.cN("demo",B.i0,"What is a DEMO account?","A seeded account, not a person. They exist so the app can be tested with a crowd in it before there is a real one.\n\nThey are always labelled, they will never answer you, and asking one to play on your song will not go anywhere. They are removed in batches as real people arrive.",B.ca1)
B.ewU=s(["/messages","messages_list"],t.s)
B.cp5=s(["message","messages","chat","thread","dm","talk","said","who"],t.s)
B.baV=new A.cN("messages",B.hb,"Who can see my messages?","A message to one person is seen by the two of you. A line in a room's thread is seen by everybody in the room, including people who join later. Nothing you say is public.\n\nYou can write to somebody you are connected with or share a room with. Blocking somebody closes the thread between you in both directions.",B.cp5)
B.caI=s(["take","back","delete","unsend","remove","edit","message","undo","sent"],t.s)
B.bb_=new A.cN("take-back",B.hb,"Can I take back something I said?","Yes. In a conversation, tap your message, then Unsend; Undo brings it back for six seconds. It goes from the chat for everybody, though a notification may already have shown it. A reply on an ask and a note have Take back beside them. There is no editing, on purpose: a changed line under somebody's answer would make the answer wrong.",B.caI)
B.exi=s(["room_call_start","call_the_room_go","call_music","in_call_bar","call_line","call_whose","room_call_needs_somebody","person_thread_more_call"],t.s)
B.bZv=s(["call","calls","video","facetime","zoom","camera","ring","remote","webcam","rehearse","room","band","start"],t.s)
B.baP=new A.cN("calls",B.hb,"How do I call my room?","Open the room and press Call the room, or Call on the room's thread, a song or a person. Everybody in the room is told, and joins from the room page, where it says who is already in.\n\nOn your own in a room, its page and its thread say Call the room: needs one more person, which opens Invite. In a thread with one person, Call rings the room the two of you share: straight in when it is just the two of you, and asked first when it is a band. With no room shared, it offers to start one, and you can call once they say yes.\n\nA call is for talking, watching each other play and rehearsing. It is not for playing live together: the others hear you a moment late. To play together, put the song up. Everybody plays to their own copy, and Record a pass keeps each person's part, lined up with the song afterwards.\n\nCall the room rings in one tap and you stay where you are. The line under the top bar says who it is ringing, then who is on the call with you, and its words open the call. Back from the call keeps it going. End, on that line or on the room's gold, asks first, then hangs up; on the call, Leave hangs up. Calls are for the people in your room, from 13: the first time, you say the month and year you were born, once. Under 18, a call that is just you and one adult waits for somebody else, with sound and video off, and you leave it after two minutes if nobody comes. Calls with just an adult and somebody under 18, and lessons, are for people 18 and over for now. The call itself is never recorded. No microphone or camera? You can still join, listen and watch. Playing along? Press Music mode and wear wired headphones.\n\nWhile somebody on Studio in a room of up to eight is on its call, the call is on their Studio plan, and it says so under the room's name. Nobody else's own calls are used while it is.",B.bZv)
B.exL=s(["room_call_start","call_leave"],t.s)
B.cvj=s(["call","end","ended","ends","dropped","hung","stopped","disconnected","paused","kicked","itself","alone","timed","timeout"],t.s)
B.b9Z=new A.cN("a-call-ended",B.hb,"Why did my call end by itself?","A call only ends by itself when nobody is using it. If you are the only one in it and nothing has happened for a while, a line on the call asks whether to keep waiting. If everybody has gone quiet for a long while, it asks whether to keep the call open. A call that has run a whole long day asks whether to keep going. One tap on the line carries on, and nothing ends while anybody is playing or while your phone is recording.\n\nIf nobody answers, the call ends and says why. Press Call the room to start another.\n\nCalls on an account can also pause until the first of the next month, once that month's calls are used. A line on the call says so shortly before, and the month running out never ends a call you are already on. Until the first you can still join a call that somebody on Studio in your band has going, because it is on their Studio plan; it ends for you a few minutes after it stops being theirs, and says so first.",B.cvj)
B.ewx=s(["/your-code","meet_qr","meet_typed"],t.s)
B.ccO=s(["scan","qr","meet","met","gig","concert","connect","add","friend"],t.s)
B.baq=new A.cN("your-code",B.hb,"How do I add somebody I just met?","Show them your code: in Account, More has Your in-person code, or Messages, then More, then Your in-person code. Their phone camera opens your card and they ask to add you; scan theirs back, or press Add back, and you are connected.\n\nCamera will not scan? Type their code (it looks like k7m2-9xqp) under Your code, or into Join with a code, under any More's Everything else.",B.ccO)
B.ewr=s(["more_else_join_with_a_code","join_code_field"],t.s)
B.czr=s(["code","link","paste","invitation","joining"],t.s)
B.b9Y=new A.cN("join-code",B.hb,"Somebody gave me a code or a link. Where does it go?","Open the link and it takes you there. To type or paste it instead: More or Tools, then Everything else, then Join with a code, on any screen. It takes an invitation, a teacher's lesson code, or somebody's own code. An invitation opens only for the address it was sent to; signed in with another, you can ask whoever sent it to send it again.",B.czr)
B.ex9=s(["more_else_invite_students","lesson_new","lesson_link_more_print_a_poster","learn_teach"],t.s)
B.cde=s(["teach","teacher","lesson","lessons","student","students","pupil","tutor","poster"],t.s)
B.bae=new A.cN("lessons",B.yZ,"How do I teach lessons in CoLabRoom?","Learn \u2192 More \u2192 New lesson link (on Learn itself while you have no lessons yet); or, on any screen, More or Tools \u2192 Everything else \u2192 Invite students to lessons. Each link is a QR code, which prints as a poster, and you can keep several, named for what they open: Tuesday beginners, Jazz studio. Every student who opens one gets their own room with you, private to the two of you. A link marked as a class also puts everybody who opens it in one room with the whole class, to listen; they still record in their own room with you. Lesson links are for students 18 and over for now.\n\nIn a lesson, open the song, press Perform, then Lead: your student presses Follow and their sheet moves with yours. What you worked on, and at what speed, waits for them on the bell afterwards, as a row with Practise.",B.cde)
B.ex8=s(["workspace_live_button","together_lead","together_follow","together_play_for_everyone","call_join_in"],t.s)
B.cr3=s(["follow","lead","leading","together","same","sync","scroll","perform","along","sleep","sleeps","asleep","awake","timeout","dim","dims","stand","phone","place","song"],t.s)
B.b9U=new A.cN("follow",B.hb,"How do we all see the same place in a song?",'Open the song on each phone and press Perform. One of you presses Lead; everybody else sees "\u2026 is leading this song" and presses Follow. The place in the song, the part on repeat and the speed then move for everybody together.\n\nOn a call, put the song up and press Play for everyone: it starts from the same place on every phone in the call that has the song up, and anybody on the faces gets a line with Join in. Your own Pause puts you on your own; Join in brings you back. Stop, on the phone playing it, stops it for everybody at the same bar. Each phone plays its own copy, so you still hear each other a moment late.\n\nWhile Perform is open, while you are in a call, and while a take is recording, the screen stays on by itself. It goes back to your usual timeout when you leave.',B.cr3)
B.exJ=s(["practice_gold"],t.s)
B.cAr=s(["practise","practice","homework","speed","slow","slower","repeat","loop","teacher","left"],t.s)
B.bb7=new A.cN("practise",B.yZ,"Where is the practice my teacher left?","On Learn, under your teacher's name, tap the song: the practice opens with the parts, the speed and your teacher's words, and its gold plays those parts at that speed. Its Tools can take it off Learn on this phone, and put it back.",B.cAr)
B.ewV=s(["workspace_layers_button","moment_note_pin"],t.s)
B.cAC=s(["note","notes","moment","pin","pinned","comment","feedback","timestamp","playhead","mark"],t.s)
B.baH=new A.cN("moment-note",B.dR,"How do I comment on one moment of a recording?",'Open the song, press Takes and play it. Stop on the part you mean, press Tools, and press "Note at 1:48" \u2014 the clock is wherever the playhead is. On a laptop, N does the same. Or press Say it instead, talk, and press Stop.\n\nThe note shows as a mark on that recording and in the list underneath. Tapping it plays from three seconds before and goes round until you press stop. Only whoever played that take is told, and you can take your own notes back.',B.cAC)
B.ey0=s(["more_else_tuner","learn_more_tuner","tune_up_tuner","live_tuner"],t.s)
B.bxF=s(["tuner","tune","tuning","sharp","flat","cents","string","strings","pitch","intonation"],t.s)
B.bar=new A.cN("tuner",B.kV,"Where is the tuner?","On Your music, press More, then Everything else, then Tuner. On Learn, press More, then Tuner. It is on every song too \u2014 press Tools, then Everything else, then Tuner \u2014 and in Perform, press Tools, then Tuner.\n\nNo song and no recording are needed. Play one string or sing one note and it names it, and says how far out you are in cents and in words: a little, quite or very flat or sharp. Once you have said what you play, it says which way to go as well: tighten or loosen on a guitar, ukulele or bass, up or down on a horn. Nothing you play is recorded.\n\nPlaying with a band at 442, or a baroque group at 415? In Tune up, press Tools, then Reference pitch. This phone remembers it, and the drone follows it.",B.bxF)
B.ex2=s(["more_else_tuner","learn_more_metronome","tune_up_metronome","live_metronome"],t.s)
B.cbP=s(["metronome","click","tempo","bpm","beats","pulse","counting"],t.s)
B.baB=new A.cN("metronome",B.kV,"Where is the metronome?","On Your music, press More, then Everything else, then Tuner, then Metronome. On Learn, press More, then Metronome. Also on every song: Tools, then Everything else, then Tuner.\n\nIn Perform it is behind the timer button on a song with no beat of its own: words or a chart with no recording, or a recording nobody has made the song sheet for. A song whose sheet found its beat counts you in at that tempo instead.\n\nTap the tempo or slide to it, and choose how many beats are in a bar. Opened on a song whose recording has been analysed it starts at that song's tempo and says so; anywhere else it starts where you last left it.\n\nFrom Tune up it stops when you close it, so it can never land on a recording. In Perform it keeps going while you read, until you leave Perform. Takes has its own click for recording a part against. The click is not in the browser yet.",B.cbP)
B.exE=s(["more_else_tuner","tune_up_drone","sheet_reach_sound_the_one"],t.s)
B.cii=s(["drone","tanpura","tonic","sa","held","warm","starting","fifth","sing","hear","note"],t.s)
B.bah=new A.cN("drone",B.kV,"Can I hear one note to sing or tune against?",'Yes. On Your music, press More, then Everything else, then Tuner, then Drone. Also on every song (Tools, then Everything else, then Tuner), inside the tuner, and in Perform.\n\nOn a song whose key is known, the song sheet\'s Tools has "Sound the 1": it holds that note until you tap it again. Anywhere else you choose the note yourself \u2014 nothing is guessed about a song nobody has said the key of.\n\nChoosing a note sounds it. With no song open it keeps your note, so next time it opens on the same one.\n\n"Starting pitch" sounds it once, for coming in on. "Fifth" adds the note a tanpura or a pitch pipe sounds over it. The slider is how loud it sits under you. From Tune up it stops when you close it; in Perform it keeps going under the song until you leave Perform. It is only ever on your own phone \u2014 nobody else in the room hears it.',B.cii)
B.exI=s(["live_practice_row","live_tempo","live_page_loop"],t.s)
B.cx0=s(["practise","practice","recorded","unrecorded","passage","loop","round","song","bars"],t.s)
B.ba_=new A.cN("practise-no-recording",B.dR,"Can I practise a song nobody has recorded?",'Yes. Open the song, press Perform, and the practice row is under Start on every song.\n\nWith no recording it holds Tempo, Count in and Loop. Tempo opens the metronome, where you tap the speed or slide to it; that number is used for this sitting and kept nowhere. Count in counts you in on that tempo \u2014 one bar, or two if you ask for two behind the timer button at the top. Loop asks which line the passage starts and ends on and how many bars it runs, and the page then comes round at your tempo.\n\nWith a recording nobody has made the song sheet for, the row holds the speeds and "Loop from here": press it where the passage starts, then again where it ends, and the recording goes round.\n\nWhat is missing is still in the row \u2014 Bars, Sing, Parts \u2014 and tapping one says what it needs. Most of them need the song sheet, and the sheet needs a recording.',B.cx0)
B.exK=s(["/settings/notifications","notify_messages"],t.s)
B.cr4=s(["notifications","notify","alerts","push","buzz","mute","quiet","silence","annoying"],t.s)
B.bao=new A.cN("notifications",B.i0,"How do I stop notifications, or get them?","In Account, open Sign-in and phone, then Notifications. Each kind has its own switch: invites, answers to your invites, being asked, messages, calls and new takes. Turning one off stops the announcement, not the thing: a message is still in Messages.\n\nNothing arriving on your phone at all? The same screen says whether this phone can be reached, and what to change if not.",B.cr4)
B.ewo=s(["/","needs_the_phone_choose_a_file"],t.s)
B.cAU=s(["computer","laptop","desktop","browser","web","website","pc","mac","windows","chrome","use"],t.s)
B.baa=new A.cN("web",B.i0,"Can I use CoLabRoom on a computer?","Yes: app.colabroom.com, signed in with the same account. Your rooms, songs, messages and calls are all there, and on a big screen the song sits beside the list. A recording you already have comes in as a file, for a song or as a take.\n\nA few things need the app on your phone: recording a song or a take, mixing takes together, the click, Feel the beat, saving a copy of the takes, sending a ChordPro file, and being told about things while the app is closed. On a computer, what is new is in the bell.",B.cAU)
B.exV=s(["/people","messages_more_your_people"],t.s)
B.cdx=s(["people","friends","connections","bandmate","online","presence","green","dot","who","invisible"],t.s)
B.bax=new A.cN("your-people",B.hb,"Who counts as my people?","Everybody you share a room with, and everybody who accepted a connection. A band-mate is one of your people whether or not they ever answered a request. Your people can see whether you have the app open right now, and you can see the same of them; nobody else can, and nobody you have blocked. To be seen by nobody, turn on Appear away in Account, under Privacy and safety.\n\nFind them on the Messages tab: More, then Your people, which is the People screen.",B.cdx)
B.exS=s(["top_bar_bell"],t.s)
B.cfl=s(["away","happened","missed","news","feed","cards","strip","unread","badge","inbox","cut","held","waiting","answered","bounce"],t.s)
B.bb8=new A.cN("what-came-in",B.hb,"How do I see what happened while I was away?","The bell, top right. Whatever came in is a row there, newest first: a take somebody recorded on your song, playable from the row without opening anything; a mix or a bounce somebody sent back; a line of yours somebody cut, with the words under it; a song of yours that cannot go out yet because somebody with a part on it has not answered, with their names; and the notes from this week\u2019s calls. While somebody needs you, the line under Your music says so.\n\nThe number on the bell is what is waiting: an ask until you answer it, anything else until you have opened the bell.\n\nNothing is lost when a row goes. A cut line stays on that song\u2019s own list, under Lines cut from this song in the song\u2019s Tools; who a held song is waiting on stays on the song (its Tools: Share and who can hear it, then Who can hear this); and every take stays on the song\u2019s Takes screen.",B.cfl)
B.ewN=s(["workspace_layers_button","seal_it","seal_opens_on"],t.s)
B.cDK=s(["seal","sealed","sealing","capsule","bury","reopen","anniversary","later","away","given"],t.s)
B.bap=new A.cN("sealed-take",B.kV,"Can I put a recording away and be given it back later?","Yes, on a take of your own that the room has not heard yet. Open the song, press Takes, tap that take, press Tools, and press Put away until a date.\n\nYou choose the day it comes back: a year from now, or Another day for any day from tomorrow to just short of ten years. Until then it is out of the song's takes and the mix, nobody else can see it, and it is not deleted. On Takes one line under the takes says until when, and Open it early beside it brings it back sooner.\n\nOn that day the song's row on Your music says so, with Play it, once. Playing it ends the seal; the take itself is still there.",B.cDK)
B.ey4=s(["workspace_layers_button","layers_record_button","takes_count_in"],t.s)
B.c5t=s(["punch","punched","punching","middle","cold","count","song"],t.s)
B.bab=new A.cN("punch-in",B.kV,"Does it count me in when I record from the middle of a song?","Yes, once the song sheet has found the bars, which the full analysis does. Open the song, press Takes, tap the song's bar where you want to come in, and press Record from there: the song counts you in at its own tempo with a click, and you come in on the top of that bar rather than exactly where the playhead was sitting. A take from the beginning is counted in too, and the song starts from the top after the count. Tools, then Count-in and pedal, sets how long the count is.\n\nA song whose bars have not been found, and a song with nothing on it yet, are counted in too: the same number of beats at the click's tempo, which Click tempo in Tools sets. There is no bar of the song to move you to there, so the take starts exactly where the playhead was. A tap on Stop during the count stops it, and nothing is recorded.",B.c5t)
B.ex_=s(["workspace_layers_button","takes_take_turns","take_turns_skip"],t.s)
B.cep=s(["turns","swap","queue","conversation","skip","same","bars"],t.s)
B.baE=new A.cN("take-turns",B.dR,"Can we all have a go at the same few bars?","Yes. Open the song, press Takes, then Tools, and Take turns recording. Pick the passage in bars and the order, and anybody in the room can take one.\n\nEach person records over the same bars on their own phone, one after another, and the app lays the turns end to end so the whole thing plays back as one conversation. Skip me is always free and you can go again afterwards. Nothing about it is scored, counted or ranked.",B.cep)
B.ewH=s(["live_loop_bars","live_this_is_bar_one","live_count_a_cycle","chart_this_is_bar_one"],t.s)
B.cgR=s(["downbeat","downbeats","cycle","sam","tala","struck","bar","bars","count"],t.s)
B.ba3=new A.cN("bar-one",B.dR,"The bar numbers are not the ones we count. Can I change them?",'Yes, and in two ways. Open the song, press Perform, then Bars.\n\n"This is bar 1" writes down where the band counts from, on the bar the picker is showing. Everybody in the room counts from there afterwards, and "Use the detected bars" puts it back.\n\n"Count a cycle" is for a song that does not go round in fours: tap how many beats it goes round in and which of them are struck hardest, and the sheet counts cycles instead of bars. It is offered only where a cycle would begin on a beat the recording actually has, because putting the 1 anywhere else would write down a beat nobody pointed at.\n\nA chart you brought carries the same "This is bar 1".',B.cgR)
B.exD=s(["workspace_live_button","perform_more_start_from_a_part"],t.s)
B.c9L=s(["letter","letters","rehearsal","bridge","jump","start"],t.s)
B.bau=new A.cN("rehearsal-letters",B.dR,"How do we start from letter B?","Open the song, press Perform, then Tools, then Start from a part. Once the song sheet knows the song's parts they are listed by letter \u2014 A, B, C, with I for an intro and O for an outro. The part the song is in says Now, and one tap starts from that letter.\n\nThe same letters are on the printed chord chart and in a set's stand-in pack, so the letter somebody calls out is the letter on the paper in front of them.",B.c9L)
B.exU=s(["copy_link_to_playhead","live_copy_moment","moment_note_pin"],t.s)
B.caJ=s(["link","copy","clipboard","spot","exactly","exact"],t.s)
B.baC=new A.cN("moment-link",B.dR,"How do I send somebody the exact spot in a recording?",'Open the song, press Takes, stop where you mean, press Tools, and press "Copy link to 1:48" \u2014 the clock is wherever you stopped. In Perform the same thing is "Copy link to here". Every note pinned to a moment carries its own link as well.\n\nWhat you paste opens the song at that second, on that recording, for anybody in the room. For anybody else it opens nothing and says so: there is no public page for anything inside a room.',B.caJ)
B.ey_=s(["song_sheet_key_badge","key_reference_sheet"],t.s)
B.ceo=s(["capo","fret","frets","barre","clamp"],t.s)
B.baR=new A.cN("capo",B.dR,"Where do I put the capo?","On the song sheet, tap the key at the top of the sheet. The sheet that opens lists the frets and what each one gives you, and the row for this song says it in this song's own chords: \"Capo 3 makes these open shapes: G, C, D\".\n\nIt is worked out for the instrument you said you play, so a ukulele gets the ukulele's answer rather than the guitar's. Choosing a capo there moves the shapes on the sheet and leaves the key the song sounds in alone.",B.ceo)
B.eww=s(["sheet_reach_language","song_language_search","song_language_not_said"],t.s)
B.chB=s(["language","languages","sung","arabic","hindi","spanish","song"],t.s)
B.baj=new A.cN("song-language",B.dR,"How do I say what language a song is sung in?","On the song sheet, press Tools, then Words & fixes, then Language, and pick a language, or type one that is not listed. Anybody who can edit the song can set it, and everybody in the room reads the same answer.\n\nNothing is guessed. Until somebody says, no language is set. Once it is said, the app tells the transcriber which language to listen for instead of letting it decide from the first few seconds.",B.chB)
B.exZ=s(["workspace_live_button","live_countdown_settings"],t.s)
B.cCR=s(["vibrate","vibration","vibrates","haptic","deaf","feel","tap","phone"],t.s)
B.ba5=new A.cN("feel-the-beat",B.dR,"Can the phone tap the beat so I can feel it?","Yes, on a song whose sheet has been made. Open the song, press Perform, then the timer button at the top of the screen: Feel the beat taps the song's own beat while it plays, heavier on the 1.\n\nIt is off until you turn it on, it is on your own phone only, and nobody else in the room feels or hears anything.",B.cCR)
B.cxr=s(["spoken","speaks","aloud","ahead","coming","announced","blind"],t.s)
B.baX=new A.cN("hear-the-chords",B.dR,"Can it say the chords aloud, a beat ahead?","Yes, on a song whose sheet has been made. Perform, then the timer button at the top: Hear the chords coming says the next chord a beat before it arrives, in whatever reading you are on \u2014 letters, Nashville numbers or numerals.\n\nOff until you turn it on, and on your own phone only.",B.cxr)
B.exd=s(["bring_a_chart_door","bring_a_chart_paste","line_up_the_chart","practise_the_chart"],t.s)
B.cu9=s(["chart","chordpro","bring","brought","cover"],t.s)
B.bb1=new A.cN("brought-chart",B.dR,"I already know the chords. Can I bring my own chart?",'Yes. Open the song, press Song Sheet, and Bring a chart. Paste one, open a file, or type it: chords over the words, chords on their own, ChordPro, or chords written in brackets all read.\n\nA chart you find in a browser can be sent straight into CoLabRoom with the phone\'s own share button.\n\nWith a recording on the song, "Line it up with the recording" puts the chart on the beat so Perform can scroll it. Without a recording it still prints, and Perform still practises from it.',B.cu9)
B.ewI=s(["room_call_start","call_put_song_up","stage_song","stage_faces","together_play_for_everyone"],t.s)
B.cen=s(["stage","faces","everyone","watch","together","song"],t.s)
B.baw=new A.cN("the-stage",B.hb,"Can everyone on a call see the song together?","Yes. Open the room, press Call the room, and in the call press Put the song up. The song takes the screen \u2014 the chords and words moving in time, or the chart somebody brought \u2014 and the faces become a strip along the top.\n\nThe song never goes over the call. Each phone plays its own copy, so it is full quality for everybody; what travels is where the song is and how fast. How you read it stays yours, so a student can read numbers while the teacher reads chord names, on the same bar at the same second.\n\nPlay for everyone, above the song's controls, starts it on every phone in the call that has it up; everybody else gets a line with Join in.",B.cen)
B.exR=s(["stage_faces","stage_first_line"],t.s)
B.ciN=s(["floor","loudest","duck","drowned","everybody","once"],t.s)
B.bav=new A.cN("the-floor",B.hb,"Everybody is playing at once. Can one person be heard?","On the Stage, tap your own face: it says Take the floor. While you have it the other voices go under you rather than off, and tapping it again hands it back.\n\nTap somebody else's face to ask them to take it. Their phone accepts \u2014 nothing is switched on from your end, ever.",B.ciN)
B.exw=s(["call_walk_line","call_back_to_the_room"],t.s)
B.c5P=s(["walk","privately","aside","quietly","talk","student"],t.s)
B.bb4=new A.cN("walk-the-room",B.yZ,"In a class, can I talk to one student without the rest hearing?","Yes, if you are the teacher. In the call, tap that person's tile: you step over to them and only the two of you hear each other. \"Back to the room\" brings you out again.\n\nEvery phone in the call shows a lamp on the tile of whoever the teacher is with, the student's own phone included. There is no silent listening in.",B.c5P)
B.exF=s(["stage_record_a_pass","stage_hear_the_band","stage_pass_not_me"],t.s)
B.bWr=s(["pass","apart","simultaneously","yourselves","part"],t.s)
B.baT=new A.cN("the-pass",B.kV,"Can we each record our own part in one pass?","Yes, on the Stage. Press Record a pass: everybody who says yes records themselves, on their own phone, over the same part of the song. When it ends, Hear the band plays back what came in.\n\nNone of it goes over the call. Each phone places its own take against its own copy of the song, which is why the parts line up without any two phones ever agreeing on an instant. Anybody can say no to a pass, and then nothing on their phone records.",B.bWr)
B.ex1=s(["live_we_said","we_said_body","song_what_we_said"],t.s)
B.c90=s(["quote","quotes","agreed","decisions","decided","down","bar"],t.s)
B.b9Q=new A.cN("we-said",B.dR,"How do we write down what the band decided about a bar?",'Open the song, press Perform, and press "We said" \u2014 it carries the bar you are on, so stop where you mean first. Type it, or hold the button and say it out loud into your own phone.\n\nWhat you leave is a quote with a name on it. Nothing summarises it, tidies it, turns it into an instruction or crosses it off: changing the chart stays a separate, deliberate act by somebody who can edit the song. Everything the band has said is listed on the song itself: Tools, Chat about this song, Call notes on this song.',B.c90)
B.ey1=s(["/openmic","open_mic_play_with_me","play_along_words"],t.s)
B.cat=s(["proposal","propose","stranger","strangers","ask","open","mic"],t.s)
B.ba8=new A.cN("play-with-me",B.lS,"Can I ask somebody from the Open Mic to play with me?",'Yes. Open the Open Mic, open their song, and press "Play this with me" under it. It proposes one session together on a call, on that song, rather than work they take away and do alone.\n\nThe terms are on the card before you send it and again before they answer: voice first with cameras off until each of you turns yours on, nothing recorded, and either of you can leave, which is the end of it. If they let it pass you are not told and nothing is kept.\n\nThe button is there whatever the answer would be \u2014 a door that appeared only for the people allowed through it would say out loud who they are. Both of you have to be adults.',B.cat)
B.exX=s(["add_gallery_pictures","add_video_link","video_url_field"],t.s)
B.cDJ=s(["gallery","pictures","picture","photo","photos","videos","youtube"],t.s)
B.b9W=new A.cN("gallery-and-videos",B.lS,"Can I put pictures or videos on my page?","Yes. On Account, tap your name: near the bottom of your page there is Add pictures and Add a video link. Both are there whether or not you have put anything up yet.\n\nA picture can be tied to one of your songs, and then tapping it plays the song. A video is a link to wherever it already lives: nothing is uploaded and nothing is hosted here.",B.cDJ)
B.exT=s(["call_add_camera","add_camera_qr","hands_begin"],t.s)
B.chD=s(["hands","camera","fretboard","angle","tripod","overhead","fingers","phone"],t.s)
B.bat=new A.cN("your-hands",B.hb,"Can a second phone show my hands on a call?","Yes. In the call, press Add a camera. A code comes up, and your own second phone's camera opens it \u2014 it has to be signed in as you. That phone joins as your hands, beside your face in the strip, and a tap puts it up large over the song.\n\nIt is never flipped left to right, because a mirrored fretboard is the wrong shape to copy.",B.chD)
B.exj=s(["song_who_was_in_the_room","split_keep","split_print"],t.s)
B.bLm=s(["split","splits","wrote","writers","cowriters","cowrote","royalties","shares","songwriting","publishing","sheet"],t.s)
B.baU=new A.cN("splits",B.dR,"How do we work out who wrote the song and how to split it?","Open the song, press Tools, then Finish, rename or delete, and Who wrote and played it. It lists everybody the room recorded on the song, with the lines each of them wrote and the takes each of them played beside their name. Nothing is counted or scored.\n\nUnder that is a draft of the writers' split. The room's owner, or somebody who can record and edit, marks who the writers are, including somebody who wrote the music and never typed a word. Everybody starts equal, and you change the numbers by hand until they add up to 100. It is about the song itself, not about a recording of it, and nobody signs anything here: Print makes a copy marked DRAFT to take into the conversation.\n\nOn somebody else's song there is nothing to split, and the page says so.",B.bLm)
B.ewF=s(["song_the_record","takes_main_take","the_record_list"],t.s)
B.cch=s(["master","mix","mixdown","bounce","version","versions","final","demo","mastered"],t.s)
B.bb5=new A.cN("the-record",B.dR,"How do we make the mix, or one take, the song?","Open the song, press Takes, then Tools, and Main take: choose the recording that is the song. On Takes, tap any take and press Make this the main take. Any take, a file you added from a DAW, or the song's own recording can be the record. The room hears it as the song straight away.\n\nAnybody else whose part may be on it is asked first, on the same card as putting the song on the Open Mic. Until they say yes, people outside the room go on hearing what they heard before. Their answer is about that recording only: what they said about their own takes stays as it was, and they can change it on the record's page with Put my part on it or Take my part off it. Somebody else's song keeps its record with the room.\n\nEvery version stays on the page, in the order it was made the record, with its date and who chose it. Not the record after all takes one back. The room's owner, anybody who can record and edit in it, and whoever started the song can choose; everybody in the room can listen. The song sheet stays with the recording it was read from until you press Read it from the record.",B.cch)
B.ex3=s(["song_let_people_use_it","use_sheet_tell_us"],t.s)
B.cAi=s(["film","films","advert","adverts","commercial","licensing","placement","placements","filmmaker","videographer","soundtrack"],t.s)
B.ba6=new A.cN("let-people-use-it",B.dR,"Can other people use our song in a film or an advert?","Not yet. On a song marked finished, press Tools, then Share and who can hear it: Let people use it is there, and What can I do lists it too. It shows, line by line, what it would take for other people to be allowed to use the song: whose song it is, whether everybody on it has said yes to being heard, who wrote it and who played, and what is still to come. A film team that needs a signed music release can have one now: Who wrote and played it prints it, under the writers' split.\n\nNothing on it commits the song to anything. Where a line waits on something you can already do here, like saying who wrote it, tapping the line takes you there. What you made stays yours, nothing happens until every person on it says so, and everybody on the song sees the same list. Marking a song finished, or putting it on the Open Mic, never signs it up for this. At the bottom of the list you can tell us what you think it is.",B.cAi)
B.ewM=s(["room_print_a_release","release_print"],t.s)
B.ceI=s(["release","releases","festival","festivals","clearance","team","teams"],t.s)
B.baf=new A.cN("music-release",B.dR,"A film team needs a music release. Can the app make one?","Yes. Open the song, then Tools, Finish, rename or delete and Who wrote and played it, and under the writers' split tap \"Somebody wants this in their film? Print a release.\". What can I do lists it too, as Print a music release.\n\nIt is filled in from the song: its title, the writers and their shares, who played, and the recording. You type who it is for and each person's legal name, which go on the page and are not kept anywhere. Everybody signs the paper themselves. CoLabRoom is not a party to it, has not checked it, and it is not legal advice.\n\nIt prints for a finished song you wrote, once the writers' split adds up to 100, and everybody on it has to have said they are 18 or over.",B.ceI)
B.ewS=s(["workspace_live_button","live_reel_cut"],t.s)
B.bVZ=s(["reel","reels","clip","clips","instagram","tiktok","trailer","seconds","cutdown","cutdowns"],t.s)
B.baK=new A.cN("reel-cut",B.dR,"How do I cut 30 seconds of my song for a reel?","Open the song and press Perform. In the practice row is \"Cut for a reel\", for a film too. Pick one of the three lengths and the app offers up to three cuts, its first choice at the top. Each starts on the 1 of a bar, is never longer than the length you picked, and ends like an ending \u2014 the song's own ending, the end of a part where the song falls back, or the song's own last bar or bars joined on where a phrase ends. Press play to hear one, and Save this one to send it on as a wav.\n\nIt needs the song\u2019s bars: the ones a full analysis finds, or the cycle your band counts. Somebody else's song is never cut: its recording stays here.",B.bVZ)
B.exW=s(["/settings/licences","account_licences_row","auth_licences"],t.s)
B.bKN=s(["licence","licences","license","licenses","source","attribution","acknowledgements","notices","typeface","fraunces","built"],t.s)
B.bay=new A.cN("licences",B.i0,"Where are the open-source licences?","Account \u2192 Help and legal \u2192 Open-source licences. It shows the licences of the open-source software this app is built from, and of its typeface, Fraunces.\n\nBefore you have an account, the same page is on the sign-in screen: More, then Everything else, then Help, then Open-source licences.",B.bKN)
B.ewu=s(["songs_ideas_see_all","ideas_search","ideas_select","keep_it_for_later","take_keep_it_for_later"],t.s)
B.ccM=s(["ideas","kept","keep","later","thing","drafts","deleted","expire","forever","unsure","folder"],t.s)
B.baz=new A.cN("kept-for-later",B.kV,"Where is what I kept for later, and will my ideas be deleted?","In Ideas, first on Your music, with See all at the end of its heading. What you record with Record an idea (REC, the red key in the bar of tabs; New idea on a wider screen), or write down, goes there, and so does anything you keep for later. Leaving Record an idea asks Save this recording?, and Save it in Ideas keeps it; Keep it for later is beside Throw it away when you cancel a song's own recording, and beside Delete on a take you recorded, and what it keeps is named for the song it came from.\n\nNothing in Ideas is deleted by a clock. It is kept until you delete it: tap an idea and choose Delete this idea, or choose Select several from More to delete or move several at once. It asks first, and Undo is there for six seconds before anything goes. Move to a room, on the same sheet, moves an idea into one of your rooms.\n\nUntil there is signal, something you kept is only on this phone, and its row in Ideas says so; it goes in by itself when the signal is back. In a browser there is nowhere to keep a recording, so there Cancel throws it away.",B.ccM)
B.ey3=s(["/settings/blocked","account_blocked_row","call_block"],t.s)
B.c7E=s(["block","blocked","blocking","unblock","unblocking"],t.s)
B.ba1=new A.cN("blocked-people",B.i0,"How do I block somebody, or unblock them?","On their page, press More, then Block. In a call, press the dots in the corner of their picture, then Block. It asks once, and says what it does before it does it.\n\nAfter that they cannot find you, ask you or invite you to anything, and you do not see them either. They are never told. A room you met in through a door ends between you, unless it is staying for good. Any other room you share stays as it is.\n\nTo undo it: Account \u2192 Privacy and safety \u2192 Blocked people, tap their name, then Unblock. That does not tell them anything either, and it does not bring back a room the block ended.",B.c7E)
B.exf=s(["/account","account_sign_out"],t.s)
B.can=s(["signout","logout","signedout","loggedout","logoff","signoff","signup"],t.s)
B.baI=new A.cN("sign-out",B.i0,"How do I sign out?","Tap More at the top right, then Everything else, then Account. Sign out is in More on Account, and at the foot of Sign-in and phone; it says Signing out while it works.\n\nSongs you kept on this phone for playing with no signal stay here, for when you sign back in; nobody else signing in sees them.\n\nTo make a different account, sign out first. On a phone, the sign-in screen has Create an account.",B.can)
B.ex4=s(["account_edit_profile","account_change_photo","account_face"],t.s)
B.bZx=s(["name","rename","avatar","photo","picture","initials","change"],t.s)
B.b9V=new A.cN("edit-profile",B.i0,"How do I change my name or my picture?","On Account, More has Your name, which changes your name. Tap your photo at the top of Account to add one; once you have one, the same tap offers Change photo and Remove photo.\n\nYour page has both as well, with what you play, what you sound like and whether people can find you: on Account, tap your name, then Edit your page.",B.bZx)
B.ewT=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row","what_you_get_standing"],t.s)
B.cB5=s(["sheets","allowance","limit","quota","month","used","many","reset"],t.s)
B.ba0=new A.cN("song-sheets-left",B.i0,"How many song sheets do I have left this month?","In Account, open Sign-in and phone, then Song sheets left this month. The card at the top says which plan you are on, how many song sheets you have made this month and how many are left. They come back on the first of the month. If it could not check, it says so, and Try again asks again.\n\nA full analysis also uses a credit, and the same page says how many of those you have.",B.cB5)
B.cgD=s(["plan","membership","stems","tier","tiers","member","add","studio","month","monthly"],t.s)
B.baQ=new A.cN("member",B.i0,"What does Studio add?","What you get (in Account, Sign-in and phone, then Song sheets left this month) puts the two side by side. A full analysis hears the words and finds the bar lines, makes separated stems, so you can hear the bass on its own or mute it and play along, and names the song\u2019s parts on the sheet. Every account starts with a few credits for those, and Studio adds more every month. And while somebody on Studio is on a call in a room of up to eight, the call is on their Studio plan rather than everybody else's.\n\nEverything else is free and stays free: rooms, recording, takes, the Open Mic, and the chords sheet, with the chords and the key and no words or bar lines. There is no way to pay for Studio in the app yet: it is $9.99 a month or $99.99 a year (save $19.89 a year), when it opens.",B.cgD)
B.ewp=s(["call_music","call_put_song_up","stage_record_a_pass"],t.s)
B.cfU=s(["behind","lag","laggy","delay","delayed","latency","late","bluetooth"],t.s)
B.b9S=new A.cN("call-behind",B.hb,"The call feels behind. Why?","Sound on a call crosses the internet, so everybody hears everybody else a moment late. No app can take that away: it is the distance and the network. It is why a call is for talking, watching and rehearsing, not for playing live together.\n\nTwo things make it worse, and both can be fixed. Bluetooth headphones and speakers add a delay of their own that you can feel, so wear wired ones. And a weak signal adds more.\n\nTo play a song together, press Put the song up in the call, then Record a pass: each of you records on your own phone, against your own copy, and the parts line up afterwards.",B.cfU)
B.exC=s(["account_email_password_row","change_email","change_password"],t.s)
B.cf4=s(["password","email","address","forgot","reset","change"],t.s)
B.bb6=new A.cN("email-and-password",B.i0,"How do I change my email or password?","In Account, open Sign-in and phone, then Email and password. Change email sends a link to the new address, and nothing changes until you open it; if a link arrives at your old address too, open that one as well. Change password asks for the new one twice, and you stay signed in on this phone.\n\nSigned out and cannot remember it? On the sign-in screen, type your email and press Forgot password. The email that comes opens CoLabRoom to choose a new one, or to keep the one you have. It comes from CoLabRoom, hello@colabroom.com.",B.cf4)
B.ewC=s(["/what-you-get","account_plan_row","what_you_get_space","what_you_get_let_go","space_full_let_go"],t.s)
B.c9a=s(["space","storage","full","paying","gb","gigabyte","gigabytes"],t.s)
B.baN=new A.cN("space",B.i0,"What happens when my space is full, or if I stop paying?","Every account has space for the recordings you add and the pictures on your page, and Studio has a lot more. What you get (in Account, Sign-in and phone, then Song sheets left this month) says how much of yours is used, with the exact figures one tap away. What the app makes from your recordings, such as stems, never counts, and nor does anything anybody else adds. A recording counts while it is yours to let go of: one you leave in a room you have left stays with that room and stops counting.\n\nWhen it is full, nothing is deleted, and everything you have still plays and downloads. Only adding new recordings waits: a take, an idea, a voice note on a line or a song\u2019s recording you make is kept on your phone, marked Only on this phone (a take says Not sent yet, on its song\u2019s Takes, and a voice note\u2019s dot beside its line turns gold), and goes up by itself, to where you made it, once there is room. Choose what to let go lists your own recordings, largest first, and says what letting one go changes before anything goes.\n\nNobody can pay for anything yet. When Studio opens, stopping will work the same way: nothing you made is deleted or locked, and only adding new recordings waits until you are back within the free plan's space.",B.c9a)
B.ewD=s(["/learn","learn_use_code","learn_teach","learn_ask","learn_more_practice_a_song","learn_more_tuner","learn_more_metronome","learn_more_what_you_play","learn_more_a_song_to_learn","learn_more_teachers_near_you","learn_more_get_chords"],t.s)
B.czG=s(["learn","learning","library","licensed","cleared"],t.s)
B.b9T=new A.cN("learn",B.yZ,"Where do I learn, find a teacher, or get songs to play?","Learn, the last tab. It is the people you learn from and teach, teachers first, each with your lesson room under their name and any song a lesson left practice on. The gold button plays the practice waiting for you, or, with none, opens Practice a song: Perform on one of your songs, to slow it down, loop a passage and count yourself in.\n\nWith no lessons yet, Learn shows your songs, each one tap from practising it; Ask the music helper, about the key, the chords and what might fit one of your songs; Join with a code, for a teacher's QR code or link; and New lesson link, for your own.\n\nEverything else is in More: Practice a song, Tuner, Metronome, What you play (your instrument and how you read a chart), Ask the music helper, a page for each person (their page, a message, a call in your lesson room, Report, Block and Stop lessons), New lesson link and Teachers near you, for adults at both ends, then A song to learn, which brings the chords you already have, and Get chords from a recording. Once you teach somebody, More holds Takes from students as well. On your Open Mic profile, Say you teach adds that fact; Take off profile removes it. Lesson notes waiting for your answer are in the Inbox, behind the bell, and in the lesson room: open the room from Learn, and its Tools holds Lesson notes, the call, Songs and sets, Members and Stop lessons. Songs you can use is not open yet.",B.czG)
B.exv=s(["song_verbs_door","song_verbs_sheet","song_options_menu"],t.s)
B.cn_=s(["everything","actions","options"],t.s)
B.bag=new A.cN("what-can-i-do",B.dR,"Where is everything I can do with a song?","Open the song, press Tools, then Finish, rename or delete, and What can I do here. It lists everything you can do to that song: practise it, record on it, read it your way, ask the room, put it up on a call, send it to a student, put it on the Open Mic, print it, or send the words by text or email.\n\nSomething you cannot do yet stays on the list, with the reason and, when there is one, the way to change it: a song with no recording says there is nothing to slow yet, with Add one beside it.\n\nTalk it over opens the room's conversation about the song, Tell somebody sends a note about it to the people you pick, and Say who wrote it is where a song is marked as yours, public domain or somebody else's. Printing and sending the words are in Tools as well: Share and who can hear it, then Print or save a PDF or Share anywhere.",B.cn_)
